  [friction] @01KJD933 (5 days ago by @claude)
    PR merged by review subagent while worker agent still editing files on same branch — local branch switches to main automatically, all pending Edit tool changes silently lost. Caused significant rework this session (re-applying all triage.spec.ts changes on new branch fix/triage-ac6-session-close-error). The review subagent and worker agent operate concurrently on the same branch in a fix cycle, creating a race condition. Potential mitigations: (1) worker agent checks for branch changes before editing, (2) ralph serializes review subagent after worker fully stops, (3) worker agent uses a local patch/stash before any branch changes.
  [friction] @01KJD6M8 (5 days ago by @claude)
    When deleting test files that cover spec ACs, kspec validate does not warn that AC annotations are being removed. This means coverage regressions are only caught during Codex review after the PR is up — requiring an extra fix commit. A pre-delete validate or a local-review gate that checks 'these AC annotations would disappear' would catch this earlier. Observed during task-delete-static-analysis-tests (PR #558): deleted web-ui-triage.test.ts removed all @interactive-triage-ui ac-1..ac-8 coverage; Codex caught it, required creating triage.spec.ts to recover.
  [success] @01KJD309R (5 days ago by @claude)
    window.__testWs pattern for Playwright WebSocket E2E: Store native browser WebSocket in window.__testWs via page.evaluate() and access it across subsequent evaluate() calls. Browser context maintains the global between calls. Enables clean helper functions (connectWebSocket, sendAndWaitForAck, subscribeAndWaitForBroadcast) without needing Playwright WebSocket interception. Used successfully in packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/api-websocket.spec.ts.
  [friction] @01KJD309N (5 days ago by @claude)
    CI check-unresolved-comments timing race in review fix cycle: When Codex posts inline review comments on a PR, we push a fix commit which triggers CI immediately. The check-unresolved-comments job runs BEFORE we resolve the Codex threads via GraphQL, causing it to fail on the new commit. Then requires manual workflow re-run. Mitigation: always resolve all review threads BEFORE pushing any fix commits during a review cycle.
  [friction] @01KJD309G (5 days ago by @claude)
    JS date validation gotcha in E2E tests: new Date("invalid") returns Invalid Date but does NOT throw. Tests using expect(() => new Date(x)).not.toThrow() or try/catch will always pass even with malformed timestamps - false positive. Always use isNaN(new Date(x).getTime()) for timestamp format validation. Caught this in api-websocket.spec.ts timestamp assertion (AC-29/@trait-websocket-protocol ac-3).
  [success] @01KJCXMR (5 days ago by @claude)
