  [friction] @01KJC3JS (6 days ago by @claude)
    Trait N/A annotations placed inside JSDoc block comments are not machine-parseable — the '* // AC:' pattern (where * is the JSDoc line prefix) does not match the scanner's '// AC:' regex. Must use standalone // AC: line comments OUTSIDE any /** ... */ block. Occurred in api-meta.spec.ts E2E tests, caught by Codex review, required fix commit.
  [friction] @01KJBW3RX (6 days ago by @claude)
    scanTestCoverage() only scanned rootDir/tests/ — missed packages/web-ui/tests/e2e/ where Playwright E2E specs with AC annotations live. Fixed by extending scan to also cover the E2E directory and .spec.ts/.spec.js file extensions. Risk: any future E2E test directory additions would silently miss coverage until the scan list is updated. Consider making E2E scan paths configurable or convention-documented.
  [success] @01KJBW3RS (6 days ago by @claude)
    GitHub PR thread resolution requires GraphQL mutation (resolveReviewThread), not REST API. REST API only supports replies. Pattern: get thread node IDs via graphql query on pullRequest.reviewThreads, then loop resolveReviewThread mutations. Reliably resolved all 7 threads in one pass.
  [friction] @01KJBTMZ (6 days ago by @claude)
    Elysia body schema validation returns 422 (not 400) before the handler runs. When writing E2E tests for daemon endpoints that have body schema validation (t.Object(...)), missing/invalid body fields return 422. If the handler also has manual validation that returns 400, the schema check fires first. Account for this in test assertions — do not assume 400 for missing body fields on Elysia-validated routes.
